@anon.a2b023d1a4e2834952d16152dce23780.631 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [519 x i8] }> <{ [519 x i8] c"A matrix.\0A\0AThe elements of a row should be separated by commas, while the rows\0Athemselves should be separated by semicolons. The semicolon syntax merges\0Apreceding arguments separated by commas into an array. You can also use this\0Aspecial syntax of math function calls to define custom functions that take\0A2D data.\0A\0AContent in cells that are in the same row can be aligned with the `&` symbol.\0A\0A# Example\0A```example\0A$ mat(\0A  1, 2, ..., 10;\0A  2, 2, ..., 10;\0A  dots.v, dots.v, dots.down, dots.v;\0A  10, 10, ..., 10;\0A) $\0A```" }>, align 1
